#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b7051104-6e23-5ab2-8779-5d54a3c3f5f5" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-270" :question/problem "Consider a spherical balloon with radius $r$. As the balloon loses air, its volume $V$ decreases. What is the best interpretation of $V'(r)$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/296/Source/Images/fe67280942729a8d2c75f11df00d3dde.png)" :question/worked-solution "The function $V(r)$ gives the volume of a sphere with radius $r$. So\n\n$$\nV'(r) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}V}{\\textrm{d}r} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in}V}{\\textrm{Change in}r}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $V'(r)$ is the rate at which the volume changes as the radius changes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063950 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2451a654-2255-5867-871d-54340dfeff81" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function in a Given Context"}] :question/id #uuid "8378ead2-9247-55a0-acc8-2e6d0874ea09" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-271" :question/problem "The function $B(s)$ models a school's budget, in dollars, given the average number of students $s$ in each grade. What is the best interpretation of $B'(30)=2\\,000$?" :question/worked-solution "The function $B'(s)$ represents the rate at which the budget is changing at the moment when the school has an average of exactly $s$ students in each grade.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nB'(30) = 2\\,000\n$$\n\nmeans:\n\n> *When the school has an average of $30$ students in each grade, its budget is increasing at a rate of $2\\,000$ dollars per student.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063951 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change"}] :question/id #uuid "750e7350-1434-56ef-80d8-7cf531108f96" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-273" :question/problem "On a particular day, the rate $E$ at which tourists enter a small country can be modeled as $E(t) = 50\\cdot 3^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, after midnight. The rate at which tourists leave the country can be modeled as $L(t)=100\\cdot 2^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is also the time in hours after midnight.\n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$?" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of tourists in the country at time $t$ is equal to the entry rate minus the exit rate at time $t$, that is,\n$E(t)-L(t)$.\n\nSince $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is ten hours after midnight, we have $t=10$. Substituting $t=10$, the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE(10) - L(10) &= 50 \\cdot 3^{0.2(10)} - 100 \\cdot 2^{0.2(10)} \\\\\n&= 450 - 400 \\\\\n&= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is $50$ tourists per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064027 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fa5bdf9-4b27-5565-9ee1-ecb9f9db4791" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Units of a Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "5831f44c-02c6-5a5b-a9e7-58c7ac36cb6d" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6112" :question/problem "A rocket is at a distance of $r(t)$ meters from the ground $t$ seconds after it is launched. What are the units of $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}$?" :question/worked-solution "We have that the height $r(t)$ is measured in meters and the time is measured in seconds.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}r(t): & meters \\\\ t: & seconds\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe derivative\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}\n$$\n\nmeasures a change in $r(t)$ over a change in $t$. So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dr}{dt}: \\mid \\frac{meters}{seconds}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}\n$$\n\nis measured in \"meters per second\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064028 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/id #uuid "0f4baedc-a28a-5b45-97d7-d7e1196b21c2" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6113" :question/problem "Howard, the manager of a sci-fi convention, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the convention, $t$ minutes after the convention has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the convention\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the convention\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the convention\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the convention $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}N(t)}{\\textrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in}N}{\\textrm{Change in}t}\n$$\n\nThus, $N'(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the convention changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the convention at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t$. That is,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = E(t) - L(t)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2451a654-2255-5867-871d-54340dfeff81" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function in a Given Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4c0a9b9-4721-5a6d-9be2-eb48f55b7237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, there are exactly $650$ users." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062976} {:answer/id #uuid "e792de43-0f2d-544d-8027-29a196ced420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of users increased by $650$ during the first $4$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062977} {:answer/id #uuid "06f6ff7b-8e7a-5020-aa4d-97dd0260d642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of users increased at a constant rate of $162.5$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062978} {:answer/id #uuid "16c0ac5d-f69e-56ff-8b67-0f900542d44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users decreased at a rate of $650$ users per hour\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"determining-a-rate-of-change\"></a>" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062979} {:answer/id #uuid "77180079-d085-5eee-a7f1-76f92c83605d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77180079-d085-5eee-a7f1-76f92c83605d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062980} :answer-field/id #uuid "10140cc1-8b23-58e0-93a5-8a495cf0fc48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062975}] :question/id #uuid "8b66dae7-140e-5116-ac81-188561d113a9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48571" :question/problem "The function $U(t)$ models the number of users of a new mobile phone app, $t$ hours after launching the app. What is the best interpretation of $U^{′}(4) = 650$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9334e32a-7902-5dc5-8710-2edb1767639d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of a rectangle with base $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063012} {:answer/id #uuid "95f5013e-834e-5464-b086-5cd8bd550c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the height changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063013} {:answer/id #uuid "9f15d574-fb5e-5d2f-a11f-688ff88c353b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the height changes\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"interpreting-the-derivative-of-a-function-in-a-given-context\"></a>" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063014} {:answer/id #uuid "a374ec78-feae-5ba2-b46f-b697e6f892dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the base changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063015} {:answer/id #uuid "b29a1b41-8848-5080-aad0-e40ee42dd1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of the base of the rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a374ec78-feae-5ba2-b46f-b697e6f892dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the base changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063015} :answer-field/id #uuid "08c21104-ac4e-5448-88ea-daebe5e7a776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063011}] :question/id #uuid "b3408555-de68-5409-ab55-f212404a9d43" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48684" :question/problem "Consider a rectangle such that the height is fixed but its base $b$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of $A^{′}(b)$ if $A$ is the area of the rectangle?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9257a3f9-f902-5951-a0d3-dcc3648fd723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063653} {:answer/id #uuid "adfb55f8-1dd2-5264-8cff-2cfb53da8dbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = r^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063654} {:answer/id #uuid "eaca6459-c7d5-512c-a227-55adcacfb17c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063655} {:answer/id #uuid "096eb4d2-7405-581c-ac78-be059cbfd79a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) =-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063656} {:answer/id #uuid "7301575d-bb4c-594d-9d18-dbc7d5952002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) =-r^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaca6459-c7d5-512c-a227-55adcacfb17c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063655} :answer-field/id #uuid "a869aa6e-9434-5eed-8b55-f676d6b8d396" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063652}] :question/id #uuid "97f8f938-0d50-59f5-922b-f7bea8bb44f7" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-72004" :question/problem "Jason, a biologist, is measuring the growth of bacteria in a Petri dish by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of bacteria in the dish.\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bacteria in the dish is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)$?"}]}
